(Definition 7 (Awareness point)) Tj
0 -16 Td
/F3 11 Tf
(AwA(t) := (aw(A,t), lev(A)).) Tj
0 -30 Td
/F4 11 Tf
(Demark 1.) Tj
0 -16 Td
/F3 11 Tf
(This is immediately a two-dimensional product space. It is not automatically a vector space: vector addition and scalar multiplication have not yet been defined.) Tj
0 -30 Td
/F4 11 Tf
(Definition 8 (Product awareness order)) Tj
0 -16 Td
/F3 11 Tf
(Aw(A) <= Aw(B) iff aw(A) <= aw(B) and lev(A) <= lev(B).) Tj
0 -30 Td
/F4 11 Tf
(Lemma 1 (Incomparability)) Tj
0 -16 Td
/F3 11 Tf
(There may exist A,B such that aw(A) > aw(B) but lev(A) < lev(B). Then neither is simply 'more aware';) Tj
0 -30 Td
/F4 11 Tf
(Corollary 1.) Tj
0 -16 Td
/F3 11 Tf
(No generally justified one-dimensional scalar preserves both coordinates.) Tj
